# Where the lead agent and the dev server may connect, and nothing else.
#
# One line per host: the name, the TCP ports it is allowed on, and why, after
# a `#`. A line without a reason is refused, so the machine boots no lead.
#
# The firewall gives the `lead` and `cwdev` users loopback and nothing else,
# DNS included (lead-egress.ts). Their only way out is the CONNECT proxy on
# 127.0.0.1:3128 (lead-proxy.ts), which they get as HTTPS_PROXY, and which
# opens a connection only to a name below, on a listed port, and for TLS only
# when the hello names that same host. The proxy matches names, never
# addresses, so a host behind a CDN admits itself and not the CDN's other
# sites.
#
# Changing this file is an image deploy (machine:deploy).

api.anthropic.com   tcp/443         # Claude Code's model API, feature flags and WebFetch safety check (Claude Code network-config page: required)
platform.claude.com tcp/443         # OAuth token exchange and refresh for the lead's sign-in (network-config page: required for every sign-in)
registry.npmjs.org  tcp/443         # bun install and bunx in the project checkout, for the lead and the dev server
github.com          tcp/443,tcp/22  # 22: git fetch of the project repo with the read-only deploy key (lead.sh core.sshCommand); 443: git over HTTPS for public repos. The lead never pushes: pushes go through the board server (routes/git-push.ts)
api.github.com      tcp/443         # bun github: dependencies, which ask its tarball API first; and gh, should a project install it (it is not in the image)
codeload.github.com tcp/443         # where api.github.com's tarball and archive downloads redirect (bun github: dependencies)
